Proposal: techniques — reference implementations with a version behind them

WIP, and a proposal rather than an implementation. Adding docs/TECHNIQUES.md.

A capability answers "can Bedrock do X". A technique is a thing we composed out of
several — an oddball accomplishment — and the question it needs answered is different:
does it STILL stand, on which versions, and how would we know without re-running it.

The mechanism worth having: a technique cites the capability ids it rests on, so when a
cited answer moves in the ledger, the technique goes SUSPECT automatically. That is a
free signal from data the repo already keeps. Running the reference implementation is
the expensive confirmation, not the detector.

